==Strategy==
This stage is fairly simple. It is identical to [[Pecking Order]], only it will take a bit longer with Beefcake Cat replacing Dagshund. Pretty much any mid-ranger and long-ranger can work in this stage. Make sure to use at least 2 meatshields also, preferably [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]]. Use spammable AoE units to take out the Gories, such as [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]], [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris/Cyborg]], or [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Kasa Jizo]]. Units like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]], [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama/Slapstick Cats]] also work. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] works as a good crowd-controller, although quite unnecessary.

Most Ubers will work in this stage, as long as they outrange Beefcake Cat. [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Aphrodite]] or [[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|Unit-02, Code 777]] can destroy this stage with their long-range attacks that demolish Professor A. Non-uber options include [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Legs]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon/King Dragon Cat]], and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic King Dragon]]. [[Catway (Super Rare Cat)|Drone Cat]] can also help tremendously in this stage, effectively countering Sir Seal, Gory Dark and Angelic Gory. Level 30s are recommended for this stage.

Stalling for money in the beginning is simple, as both Doge Dark and Sir Seal drop a decent amount. Just beware of their high magnifications. When you hit the base, use the [[Ototo Corps|Slow Beam]] or [[Ototo Corps|Iron Wall]] to prevent the Brollows from killing your units. Another way to counter the Brollows is simply sending your more disposable or weak units to trigger the boss, and send out your powerful units a bit later, preventing them from taking damage from Brollow.

Make sure you have either a Long-range attacker or a tank against red such as [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] to kill Professor A. after the spam, in case he is still alive.

